   "researcher_notes": "Real, operating (2016). Western route of the Southern Corridor (Южно-Европейский газопровод, Писаревка-Анапа), built to feed South Stream and then used for TurkStream; it is the same corridor as South Stream's Russian feed but a distinct physical pipe (not a duplicate of P0760 or of TurkStream). 63 bcm/y = South Stream offshore design; Interfax says corridor realised as TurkStream 31.5 bcm/y. Length: Interfax 880.6 km (route), ru.wikipedia/neftegaz 472 km built phase, RIA 2012 834 km plan. Diameter: neftegaz DN1420.",
